<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 28 February, from 1525 to 1993.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1525</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hernán Cortés executes Cuauhtémoc, the last Aztec emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Held captive since the fall of Tenochtitlan, Cuauhtémoc was hanged during Cortés's expedition to Honduras on a charge of conspiracy. He is honoured in Mexico as a symbol of resistance.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1784</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Wesley gives Methodism legal standing</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wesley's Deed of Declaration made a conference of 100 preachers the legal governing body of the Methodist societies. It ensured the movement could survive him, though it formally left the Church of England only later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1845</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress votes to annex Texas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The House agreed to a Senate joint resolution offering annexation to the Republic of Texas, signed by President Tyler on 1 March. Mexico broke off relations, and war followed in 1846.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1953</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Watson and Crick work out the structure of DNA</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Cavendish Laboratory in Cambridge, Francis Crick and James Watson arrived at the double-helix model of DNA, drawing on Rosalind Franklin's X-ray data. They published it in April.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1991</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gulf War ceasefire takes effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">One hundred hours after the ground offensive began, coalition forces halted operations, Kuwait having been liberated. Saddam Hussein remained in power in Baghdad.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1993</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Federal raid on the Branch Davidians begins the Waco siege</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A gun battle at the compound near Waco, Texas, killed four federal agents and six Branch Davidians. The 51-day siege ended on 19 April in a fire that killed 76 people, including children.</p></li></ol>
